# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production environment. Copy to `.env.production` ON THE SERVER and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.production.example .env.production && nano .env.production
#
# .env.production is gitignored and is read by docker-compose (env_file). It
# holds SHOPIFY_API_SECRET — treat the file as a secret: chmod 600, never commit.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Public origin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The HTTPS domain this app answers on, no trailing slash. MUST match the domain
# in deploy/Caddyfile and the URLs registered in the Shopify Partners dashboard.
#
# Everything derives from this: the OAuth callback, the Shopify webhook targets,
# and the Telenow webhook target. Changing it after merchants have installed
# breaks their webhooks until they reinstall — pick the final domain now.
#
# The variable is HOST. It is NOT SHOPIFY_APP_URL — that one is set by the
# Shopify CLI during `shopify app dev` and is read only by scripts/dev-cli.js.
# Setting SHOPIFY_APP_URL in production looks correct and silently does nothing;
# the app falls back to http://localhost:3000 and OAuth can never complete.
#
# On Render you may omit HOST entirely: RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL is injected into
# every web service and is used automatically. Set HOST explicitly once you put
# a custom domain in front, because RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL always returns the
# *.onrender.com address.
HOST=https://app.example.com

# Internal container port. Caddy proxies to this; do not publish it.
PORT=3000

# ── Shopify app credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Partners dashboard → your app → API access. The secret signs webhook HMACs and
# session tokens, so a leak lets anyone forge either.
#
# These MUST come from the LISTED app record, client_id
# 1181346b04d8d62d945cce9aa5fa90d7 (shopify.app.telenowvoiceai.toml) — not from
# the same-named duplicate 5aef351a…. Billing makes the difference fatal and
# invisible: currentAppInstallation.activeSubscriptions is scoped to the app that
# issued the access token, so credentials from the wrong record read back an
# empty subscription list for every paying merchant. Everyone looks unsubscribed,
# calls are refused, and no log line says "wrong app".
SHOPIFY_API_KEY=
SHOPIFY_API_SECRET=

# Must match [access_scopes].scopes in shopify.app.telenowvoiceai.toml, or the
# install loop re-prompts for consent on every request.
SHOPIFY_SCOPES=read_orders,write_orders,read_customers,read_checkouts,read_fulfillments

# REST Admin version for order tag/note write-backs (src/shopify.js:39).
# Separate from the library version used for OAuth + webhook HMAC, which is
# pinned in code to ApiVersion.January25.
SHOPIFY_API_VERSION=2025-10

# ── Telenow API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TELENOW_API_BASE=https://api.telenow.ai

# ── Telenow calling workspaces ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The merchant NEVER supplies a Telenow key. The app leases one per shop from a
# pool that an operator mints ahead of time (see DEPLOY.md § Key pool).
# JSON array; alternatively drop the same array in ${DATA_DIR}/keypool.json.
#
# This is as sensitive as SHOPIFY_API_SECRET — each entry is a live calling
# credential that can spend money. It is also load-bearing: an unset or
# unparseable pool is not a degraded mode, it is an outage. ensureWorkspace()
# returns null, every call route answers 503, and nothing dials. Seed it before
# the first install, and alarm when /healthz reports fewer than 5 free.
#
# ENTRY SHAPE: { ref, apiKey, numberE164, numberId, provider, country }.
#   provider  lowercase platform id — 'twilio' | 'plivo' | 'exotel' | 'vonage' |
#             'sip'. Twilio and Plivo are both first class; the app never asks a
#             merchant to choose one and never shows a carrier signup.
#   country   ISO-3166-1 alpha-2 of THE NUMBER (where the DID lives), not of the
#             merchant holding it.
#
# Both fields are optional and additive — entries seeded before they existed keep
# working — but an entry without them counts as unknown-origin, never as Indian,
# and is only ever handed out as a fallback. Label everything you seed.
#
# THE LEASE PREFERS A MATCHING COUNTRY. At install the app reads the shop's own
# country from Shopify once (cached on settings.shopCountry) and asks the pool
# for a number in it, falling back to any free entry rather than refusing to
# lease — a foreign number that connects beats a 503. So an unstocked country is
# not an outage, it is a quality problem that only shows up in the logs
# ("rule=any-free — no free US number available") and in /healthz's
# keypool.byCountry. Watch both.
#
# ★ AT LEAST TWO FREE US/CA NUMBERS MUST BE IN THE POOL BEFORE APP REVIEW.
# Shopify's reviewer works from North America and the most prominent button in
# the app is "Send a test call". An Indian DID ringing a North-American mobile is
# frequently blocked or spam-filtered by the destination carrier, so the reviewer
# does not see a slow feature — they see one that does not work, and the app is
# re-paused under requirement 2.1.1 (functionality), where none of the billing
# rework helps. Two rather than one, because install → uninstall → reinstall is
# how requirement 1.2.2 is tested and each cycle quarantines an entry.
TELENOW_KEY_POOL=[{"ref":"ws-01","apiKey":"vai_live_...","numberE164":"+14155550123","numberId":"...","provider":"twilio","country":"US"},{"ref":"ws-02","apiKey":"vai_live_...","numberE164":"+16475550123","numberId":"...","provider":"twilio","country":"CA"},{"ref":"ws-03","apiKey":"vai_live_...","numberE164":"+919876543210","numberId":"...","provider":"plivo","country":"IN"}]

# v1.1 only — server-to-server provisioning against the Telenow partner API.
# Leave unset in v1; the pool is the mechanism today, not a fallback.
# TELENOW_PARTNER_KEY=

# ── Persistence ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path INSIDE the container. Backed by the `telenow-data` Docker volume — see
# docker-compose.yml. Do not point this at a path that isn't a mounted volume.
DATA_DIR=/data

# ── Automation tuning (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Interval for the win-back / reviews / post-purchase sweeps. Default 6h.
SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS=21600000
# Set to 1 ONLY for a one-off test: it runs a sweep at boot, which places real
# calls to real customers. Leave unset in production.
# SWEEP_RUN_ON_BOOT=1

# ── Phone-number country (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# LAST-RESORT fallback for normalising a customer phone number that arrives in
# local format ("9876543210") with no country code. The country is resolved per
# shop, in this order:
#
#   explicit argument → the shop's own country from Shopify
#                     → DEFAULT_PHONE_COUNTRY → 'US'
#
# It used to be the FIRST answer, read once at module load and applied to every
# merchant on the instance. That was the multi-tenant bug: one process, one
# assumed country, so a US store's local-format numbers were dialled as Indian
# ones. It is now the third answer and only fires for a shop whose country
# Shopify could not report.
#
# Leave it unset unless every merchant on this instance genuinely sells from one
# market — a wrong value here dials wrong numbers, and it does so silently.
# DEFAULT_PHONE_COUNTRY=US
